From 16cd67f490ea363ad7ff3dc8e98246a1ad3f6d76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:22:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(importer): contract the scout identity to the wide key
 and refuse a lossy reverse

Ship 20270121000000_scout_identity_contract: drop the two narrow unique
indexes on ScoutIngestEntity and ScoutReconstructionLedger so the
five-field (coach, intent, entity_type, source_platform, source_id)
identity is the only key. One source may now exist per family and per
platform; full-tuple replays stay deduped; the wide keys, canonical
CHECKs, NOT NULL provenance, fence, RLS and rows are untouched.

The down.sql recreates the narrow keys byte-exact only when no
cross-family or cross-platform identity exists; on any collision it
raises a fixed, identifier-free 23505 before either CREATE (forward
repair only). Both directions gate on the exact catalog shape, refuse
decoys and shadow search_path redirection, and bound locks to 5s.

Remove the narrow @@unique declarations from the schema, update the
ingest/reconstruct idempotency wording and the regenerated importer
OpenAPI contract, pin the wide key in the structural guards, flip the
reconstruct fakes to the wide key, and add the isolated PG17 lane proof
(rls-g2-c-contract.spec.ts with its db/guard/harness/bootstrap/old-root
helpers) plus the G2-C decision record and runbook.
